-### Formulas
-The core of the DARBF kernel is the Mahalanobis distance $d_M$ from a point $\mathbf{x}$ to the center $\boldsymbol{\mu}$ with covariance $\boldsymbol{\Sigma}$ [S1]:
+2.  **Compute Mahalanobis Distance:**
+    For a pixel center $x'$ in the 2D image plane, calculate the Mahalanobis distance $d_M$ from the projected primitive center $\boldsymbol{\mu}'$ using the 2D covariance $\boldsymbol{\Sigma}'_i$ [S1]:
+    $$ d_M(x'; \boldsymbol{\mu}', \boldsymbol{\Sigma}'_i) = \sqrt{(x' - \boldsymbol{\mu}')^T (\boldsymbol{\Sigma}'_i)^{-1} (x' - \boldsymbol{\mu}')} $$
+    where $\boldsymbol{\mu}'$ is the 2D projection of $\mathbf{p}_i$ [S1].
 
