+5.  **Rasterization and Blending:**
+    Sort primitives by depth. For each pixel, accumulate color using alpha blending [Parent]:
+    $$ C(x') = \sum_{i \in N} \mathbf{c}_i \sigma_i(x') \prod_{j=1}^{i-1} (1 - \sigma_j(x')) $$
+    where $\sigma_i(x')$ is the effective opacity contribution of primitive $i$ at pixel $x'$ [S1, Parent].
 
-### Parameters
-*   **Kernel Type:** Select from DARBF family (e.g., Half-Cosine, Inverse MQ, Radial Cosine) [S1].
-*   **Scaling Parameter ($\xi$):** Used in Half-Cosine definition [S1].
